  <p><strong>Guaranteed indirect delivery in directed networks</strong><br/>Extremal bounds, sparse constructions, and verified finite cases.</p>
  <p>This is a {release.pages}-page research checkpoint with {release.figures} figures. It proves the vertex maximum at every order from twelve, both arc maxima at all sufficiently large budgets, the full main interval, and the final dense staircase. It gives a combined exact joint formula in a stated eventual range. The new antichain composition guarantees arbitrary outside-arrow choices and lowers the complete main-interval threshold to 115. It also sharpens the constructive constant at the Θ(n log n) scale for universal two-move delivery. Direct dense constructions settle the final band from order 20, and quantitative support reductions constrain near-extremizers. The complete extremal classification remains open. It has not been submitted to arXiv.</p>
